  "version": "0.5.5-beta.13",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.5-beta.12`\n\n### Features\n\n- make the ninth tab shortcut pick the last tab, as Chrome, Safari, Terminal and iTerm2 do, so the far end of a long tab bar is one key away; 1-8 still go by position ([4bbf7569](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/4bbf75690a91e62401e3227c8d1b3ba772c5dfbe))\n- flash the active tab when a tab shortcut picks the tab already in sight, and shake the tab bar when it names no tab, since such a shortcut changed nothing on screen and looked as if it had not fired; reduced motion keeps a colour or opacity change instead ([b3dfa844](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/b3dfa844b70efd517f0c4f3689eaded8890da3cb))\n\n### Fixes\n\n- empty xterm's hidden textarea when a control key is sent, since xterm only empties it on Enter and Ctrl+C, so after Ctrl+J (a new line in Claude Code and Codex) the macOS Pinyin IME still read the committed Chinese as context and auto-spaced the next digit or letter, starting the new line with a stray space; arrow keys, Tab, Backspace and Escape left the same stale context, printable keys keep it, and a pending IME diff is left alone so no DEL is sent ([ded0d193](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/ded0d19364dc21f1d788bd05a78135f82cede367))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.5-beta.12...v0.5.5-beta.13](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.5-beta.12...v0.5.5-beta.13)",
